From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Collins Ikechukwu <collinschristroa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:58:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] scf: ship the GeoLite database in the Docker image

Next's standalone output does not trace geo/, so the runner image had no
GeoLite database. Umami then fell back to CDN headers for the country
(Cloudflare's cf-ipcountry, derived from the full IP), and setting
SKIP_LOCATION_HEADERS would have made every lookup fail.

Copy geo/ into the runner, and create it in the builder even when
SKIP_BUILD_GEO is set so the COPY always has a source. With
SKIP_LOCATION_HEADERS=1, the country now comes from Umami's own lookup on
the IP cut to /24 or /48 (SCF_COUNTRY_ONLY).
---
 Dockerfile | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index 072154d..109af04 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -47,6 +47,9 @@ ARG SKIP_BUILD_GEO
 ENV SKIP_BUILD_GEO=$SKIP_BUILD_GEO
 
 RUN pnpm build:docker
+# SCF: geo/ holds the GeoLite database build:geo downloads. Create it even when
+# SKIP_BUILD_GEO is set, so the runner's COPY below always has a source.
+RUN mkdir -p geo
 
 # Production image, copy all the files and run next
 FROM node:${NODE_IMAGE_VERSION} AS runner
@@ -96,6 +99,11 @@ COPY --from=builder /app/prisma ./prisma
 COPY --from=builder /app/prisma.config.ts ./prisma.config.ts
 COPY --from=builder /app/scripts ./scripts
 COPY --from=builder /app/generated ./generated
+# SCF: Next's standalone output does not trace geo/, so without this the image
+# has no GeoLite database and can only take the country from CDN headers. With
+# it, SKIP_LOCATION_HEADERS=1 makes Umami look up the IP cut to /24 or /48
+# (SCF_COUNTRY_ONLY) instead of trusting cf-ipcountry.
+COPY --from=builder --chown=nextjs:nodejs /app/geo ./geo
 
 # Automatically leverage output traces to reduce image size
 # https://nextjs.org/docs/advanced-features/output-file-tracing
